    rdf:value """[ Jacopo di Barbari]
and changed my feeling of indifference to one of active dislike. However, Bernhard liked her, taking a long walk with her afterwards. It was so warm, I lay on the balcony reading  Ian Maclaren’s “Bonnie Briar Bush ,”
and watching the hills. I needed no wrap even. We began  Emma .
Tuesday, Feb. 4, 1896, Fiesole
Again a heavenly day. Bernhard spent a large part of it writing to Reinach a tome upon a certain Jacopo di Barbari drawing denied by Müntz and Ravaisson - (!!) to be such. In the evening we wrote an unfavourable review of Chaude Phillips’ “Collection of Charles I”."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 95 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1895-96> .

